WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
DuckDB has the orders. But shipping logic lives in application code. A VGI worker makes that function callable from SQL.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:20.000
DuckDB sends typed columns to the worker. The worker runs your library and sends a column of answers back.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Therefore, call the function with every order’s destination and weight. These are recorded results from the real SQL test.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Two orders lose money after shipping. But a missing quote is not free shipping, so that order stays in the review queue.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:44.000
The agent writes the worker and tests its actual SQL behavior. A failure feeds back into a repair and another test.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Choose your tools and describe the capability. Start with this fictional shipping example, then replace the rule with your own library.
